  <main_text>
    <p>Ligat, molliculum meri liquorem</p>
    <p>Infundens oleúmque: asellulo illum</p>
    <p>Imponit: comitatur ad tabernam:</p>
    <p>En en denarii tibi duo, inquit,</p>
    <p>Hospes, tinnuli: age indigentem</p>
    <p>Hunc cibo refice, &amp; mero, &amp; cubili:</p>
    <p>Vt chirurgus eum peritus artis</p>
    <p>Curet, effice: cùm redibo, reddam</p>
    <p>Quicquid solveris. Aptè &amp; eleganter,</p>
    <p>CAROLE integer, HEIC mihi videris</p>
    <p>BONO SAMARITANVS ille ZELO:</p>
    <p>Mentis munera cùm tua recordor</p>
    <p>Singula, optima maxima: attaménque</p>
    <p>Cumprimis, aliis mihiq; notæ</p>
    <p>Ardentis pietate christianâ.</p>
    <p>Nam quæ vulnera dira, noxiásque</p>
    <p>Plagas improbitatis ac scelestæ</p>
    <p>Vitæ; quas Satan, ille latro vastus,</p>
    <p>Inflixit per originis venenum,</p>
    <p>Perplures alii in suis propinquis</p>
    <p>Ridént, prætereunt, velapprobántque:</p>
    <p>Tu, ceu Samaritanus alter, illis,</p>
    <p>Zelo percitus optimo, medelam,</p>
    <p>Salutari oleo increpationis,</p>
    <p>Fragranti monitorum odore, sano</p>
    <p>Probi consilii mero, exhibere</p>
    <p>Studebas, pia verba Salomonis</p>
    <p>Volvens pectore, Thurei vapores</p>
    <p>Mulcent corda: sed increpans monénsve</p>
    <p>Fidè, non minùs est suâvis illis:</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Ghosted show-through from the facing page at the right is ignored. Some words in the lowest lines are partly obscured by the page edge; the readings "monénsve" and "suâvis" are uncertain.</notes>
